From e6bda19bba36ddb4d8bd0b7c9b4c21622280da1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Miroslav=20Mr=C3=A1z?= <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 01:24:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v1 18/22] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7125-samsung: allow non-secure
 ADSP FastRPC
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The ADSP sensor framework is reached through the non-secure FastRPC
device (/dev/fastrpc-adsp), which is only created when the domain is
marked non-secure. Without it the sensors daemon cannot attach.

Signed-off-by: Miroslav Mráz <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7125-samsung-common.dtsi | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7125-samsung-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7125-samsung-common.dtsi
index 0abb51084754..90bcab5921c0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7125-samsung-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7125-samsung-common.dtsi
@@ -481,6 +481,13 @@ &qupv3_id_1 {
 
 &remoteproc_adsp {
 	memory-region = <&adsp_mem>;
+
+	glink-edge {
+		fastrpc {
+			/* the sensors (SEE) client runs in the unsigned PD */
+			qcom,non-secure-domain;
+		};
+	};
 };
 
 &sdhc_2 {
-- 
2.55.0

